    narr:narration """Tina Team's voice here is an operational one: she frames [the four-site rollout and its hardest site](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_5), argues [why a double cutover is a different class of problem](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_15), and puts [a hard two-week number on the soak](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_17) — grounded in [what the Dockside pilot actually showed](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_19) and defended as [evidence-first rather than speed-first](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_22). Around that spine she runs a facilitator's register: short acknowledgments ([\"That's the question.\"](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_7), [\"I'm with you on that.\"](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_9)), a blunt reality-check on [nobody deciding off stale counts](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_29), and easy [concession when a proposal lightens site-team load](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_41). The profile is claim-conviction throughout, with expert/rational-persuasion power when she's pinning numbers down.""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_15> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_17> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_19> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_2> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_22> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_29> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_41> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_43> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_5> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_7> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_9> ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "A double cutover is a staffing problem and a data problem at the same time, which isn't." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_15> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "The soak is two full weeks. That's the Dockside number, and I'd hold us to it." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_17> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "it didn't flatten out until day nine or ten" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_19> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "I'd rather hold two weeks and shorten it with evidence than hold one week and discover we needed two." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_22> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Northgate is the smallest and the cleanest, Clyde is the one nobody wants to touch." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_5> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "Her dominant mode is argument-from-evidence, but she also concedes quickly and without qualification when a proposal reduces site-team work — the facilitator register sits alongside the hard-numbers register." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_41> ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_17> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The two-week soak rests on a single pilot at a single site, which she herself flags as the limit of the evidence — the claim is firm but its base is narrow by her own account." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_22> ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_19> ] ;
    narr:voiceTrait [ narr:dim "conviction" ; narr:reading "plain claim-conviction — she asserts positions directly, no hedging, but grounds them in named precedent" ; narr:text "The soak is two full weeks. That's the Dockside number, and I'd hold us to it." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_17> ] ;
    narr:voiceTrait [ narr:dim "power" ; narr:reading "expert authority via rational persuasion — she wins by citing the number and where it came from, not by pulling rank" ; narr:text "That's the Dockside number, and I'd hold us to it." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_17> ] ;
    narr:voiceTrait [ narr:dim "temporal" ; narr:reading "moves between concrete past (what the pilot showed) and concrete future (what we'll hold to) — always dated and specific, never abstract" ; narr:text "We watched the exception queue after go-live and it didn't flatten out until day nine or ten." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_19> ] ;
    narr:voiceTrait [ narr:dim "style" ; narr:reading "antithesis and parallelism — the sentence sets two terms against each other, then balances them" ; narr:text "I'd rather hold two weeks and shorten it with evidence than hold one week and discover we needed two." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_22> ] ;
